`research/kateri-tekakwitha/gen_lu_wang_source_def.py`; do not edit by hand.

On the piece `[t_i, t_(i+1)]` (`i = 0, ..., 2278`) the source is
`F(t) = (1+t) log(1+t) - t log t + t exp(-t) P_i(t)`, where `P_i` is the cubic Hermite interpolant with values
`v_i, v_(i+1)` and derivatives `d_i, d_(i+1)` at the two knots. Adjacent pieces agree at the knots.
Each rational is stored as a decimal string "numerator/denominator" and read by `parseRat`.
